Install and update (Windows)
----------------------------
Keep this folder together: the setup program copies game_files\ from the
folder it runs in. Run BLiNX2-@VERSION@-setup.exe. It installs for your user
only (no administrator rights) to %LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\BLiNX2 and adds a
Start Menu entry. Running a newer setup installs on top and keeps your
saves. Uninstall from Settings > Apps; your saves and settings stay in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\BLiNX2.

Windows may warn before running the setup program or BLiNX2.exe: they are
built on your machine and not signed. SmartScreen: "More info" > "Run
anyway". If the folder came as a .zip downloaded or copied from another
machine, right-click the .zip > Properties > Unblock before extracting
(Mark of the Web), or Windows asks again for every file.

Note: this build is tested under Proton on Linux only, not on native
Windows.

For a 60 fps look, external frame-generation tools may work but are
unsupported: https://github.com/apexJCL/blinx2-recomp/blob/main/docs/frame-generation.md

Controls
--------
A controller works as player 1. The keyboard and the mouse work too,
merged with a pad on player 1, while the game window has the focus:

  W/S/A/D         move              mouse          look (right stick)
  I/K/J/L         look too          arrows         d-pad
  Space           A (jump)          left click, R  right trigger (sweep)
  right click, F  B (action)        E              X (time control)
  C Z             white, black      left Shift     left trigger
  Q               Y
  Tab             left stick click  middle click   right stick click
  Enter Escape    START (pause)     Backspace      BACK
  numpad 8/2/4/6  move too          left Alt       walk (hold)

Focusing the window grabs the mouse; F9 frees the cursor and grabs it
again. To change a key, put the control under [input.bindings] in
config/config.toml in the data folder, for example
  a = ["Space", "J"]
(config.default.toml beside the game lists every control and key);
keyboard = false or mouse = false under [input] there turns either off.
